MID_SE_Pet_Nin_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_C_001: Aww... Why is the walk back from the bathroom\nalways so scary at night?
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_C_002: I feel like something's going to jump out at me, like\na ghost or...
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_C_003: Peter.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_C_004: A spirit of death?! Aah!
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_C_005: There are no spirits of death here. Just me.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_C_006: Ninae? Oh, I'm sorry. You startled me.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_C_007: It's an honor to be mistaken for an avatar of death.\nJust like Yu Phas.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_C_008: Oh? I thought you'd be angry at me for saying that\nabout you.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_C_009: Yu Phas is the noble Keeper of Death and Night.\nThe association is gratifying.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_C_010: Though usually I am named the Angel of Death.\nBy friend and foe alike.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_C_011: Because they're scared, right? Of how you fight\nwithout mercy.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_C_012: Though the other vulkans have named me\nBlack-Lace Ninae.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_C_013: Why do you wear black, Ninae?
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_C_014: I am in mourning. I mourn those whose deaths trace\nto me.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_C_015: Enemies, right? People you had to fight.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_C_016: And my mother. Her death is the first such traced.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_C_017: You...killed your mother? Why?
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_C_018: One life was taken. One was given. This trade was\nmy first sin.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_C_019: I go now to offer my nightly plea for these pitiable\nsouls to rest in peace.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_C_020: I am overdue. Good night.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_C_021: That's just about the creepiest "good night" I've\never heard.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_C_022: The way she looks and the way she talks... Ninae\nmight actually be a spirit of death.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_B_001: Ah! Ninae, where are you going? Is it evening\nprayer time?
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_B_002: Yes. Tonight I make my pleas at the graveyard on\nthe edge of the city.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_B_003: Do you always go to the graveyard at night?\nAren't you scared?
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_B_004: What would scare me there?
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_B_005: I'm scared just thinking about all the dead people\nthere, but that's me.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_B_006: Death is sad. But there is no scariness to it.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_B_007: Yu Phas guides the souls of the dead to their final\nrest at the Garden of Nibbana.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_B_008: Garden of Nibbana? Are we talking about the\nunderworld?
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_B_009: It is the land of purification, also called the Plateau of\nNibbana. The souls of the dead are bound for it.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_B_010: In that place, the souls are cleansed in the River\nof Forgetting. After an eternity, they return.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_B_011: It is a sacred process. This cycle has repeated for\nall eternity, and will continue forevermore.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_B_012: So the souls forget everything, and then they're\nreborn? Is that in line with temple teachings?
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_B_013: I learned it from Father. He learned it from Mother.\nShe learned it in service to Yu Phas.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_B_014: Yu Phas is the true goddess of death. I believe in\nher creed too.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_B_015: So you pray that they'll go to this Garden of Nibbana,\nthe enemy's souls and your mother's soul alike.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_B_016: I cannot guide the dead. But I can plea for their\nsafe travel. Those pitiable souls...
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_B_017: I have to be honest, Ninae. I thought you were kinda\nscary, but you're actually very kind.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_B_018: Kind? That is a strange perspective.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_B_019: You pray for the souls of those who tried to kill you,\nand you continue to pray for your mother's soul.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_B_020: And you shared with me about the Garden of\nNibbana because I was afraid.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_B_021: It makes me feel more at ease just to know that there\nare beliefs like yours out there. Thank you, Ninae.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_B_022: The learning has passed now through me to you.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_B_023: You know what? I'm gonna go to the graveyard too.\nI want to pray for those who've died.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_B_024: A noble spirit resides in you, Peter.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_B_025: Let us be off. And beware the beasts and bandits\nof the night roads.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_B_026: B-beasts and bandits? You never said anything about\nbeasts and bandits. But I guess you're always safe...
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_B_027: If they attack me, I kill them. They are added to the\nlist of my pleas to reach the Garden.
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_B_028: Just kill 'em and send 'em off to the Garden? Is it\nalright to have such a casual attitude about this?
MID_SE_Pet_Nin_B_029: Beasts and bandits are scary, but not as scary as\nNinae. What is going on in her head?